{
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "description": "Land value (Phase 6c-3, ARCHITECTURE decision 76), worked out when asked: value = clamp(floor(B x D / 1000) + 15 x S + 1000 x A, 500, 50000) cents a m2, B the use's base (1000 an empty cell, 2000 homes, 3000 shops, 3500 offices), D the building's density factor (1000, 1250, 1600, 2000 for D1 to D4, existing stock D4; 1000 without a building), S and A the best station's score floor(w x lastService / 1000) and lastReached, w = 1000 - floor(d2 x 1000 / 51200^2) for the stations whose catchment reaches the cell (d2 < 51200^2) and that measured some service, the highest score winning and a tie going to the lower station. A world 32768 x 8192 units (8 x 2 cells) on economy.json's line Main (Alpha (1536, 512), Beta (3584, 512), Gamma (5632, 512), one train all day from 23:00), managed, with demand from land, town growth and the city's buildings on. The land: row 0 column 0 homes of 100 (D2), 1 shops of 100 jobs (D2), 2 offices of 1600 jobs (D4), 3 homes of 2000 (existing stock), row 1 column 0 homes of 56 (D1). Before any service is measured each cell is worth its base: 2000 x 1250 / 1000 = 2500, 3000 x 1250 / 1000 = 3750, 3500 x 2000 / 1000 = 7000, 2000 x 2000 / 1000 = 4000, 2000, and an empty cell (row 1 column 7, row 0 column 7) 1000; cells outside the world (row 2, column 8, row -1) have none. After the first midnight (no measure yet) still 2500. The second midnight measures every station at lastService 1000 and lastReached 2 (GameCore's values from the railway, as the townGrowth observations show) and raises the full D1 homes at row 1 column 0 to D2 (decision 75). Then: row 0 column 0, middle (2048, 2048), is d2 = 512^2 + 1536^2 = 2621440 from Alpha and 1536^2 + 1536^2 = 4718592 from Beta, both w = 999 (1000 - 1, 1000 - 1): a tie, Alpha; S = 999, 2500 + 14985 + 2000 = 19485. Column 1 (6144, 2048) is nearest Gamma, d2 = 512^2 + 1536^2, w 999: 3750 + 14985 + 2000 = 20735. Column 2 (10240, 2048): Gamma, d2 = 4608^2 + 1536^2 = 23592960, floor 9, w 991: 7000 + 14865 + 2000 = 23865. Column 3: Gamma, w 971: 4000 + 14565 + 2000 = 20565. Row 1 column 0 (now D2): Alpha, d2 = 512^2 + 5632^2, floor 12, w 988: 2500 + 14820 + 2000 = 19320. The empty row 1 column 7 (30720, 6144): Gamma, d2 = 25088^2 + 5632^2, floor 252, w 748: 1000 + 11220 + 2000 = 14220; row 0 column 7: Gamma, w 759: 1000 + 11385 + 2000 = 14385. In free play the land does not set ridership and only the base counts: 2500 and 7000. Every landValue is worked out from the rule, the observed buildings and the observed measures by an independent Python implementation (tools/golden-checks/land_value.py); the railway, passenger, account and land values are GameCore's, as in economy.json.",
